# repr_enum_flags — enum with explicit representation (flags)
# (README §10). Tests enum repr for bit flags.

ReprEnumFlags is project
ReprEnumFlags module examplesReprEnumFlags
ReprEnumFlags target console
ReprEnumFlags entry main

examplesReprEnumFlags is module
examplesReprEnumFlags path examples.reprEnumFlags
examplesReprEnumFlags exports main
examplesReprEnumFlags purpose "Demonstrate enum repr for flags"
examplesReprEnumFlags invariant "Enum values can have explicit repr"

Permissions is enum
Permissions variant read repr 1
Permissions variant write repr 2
Permissions variant execute repr 4

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Use enum with explicit repr values"
main invariant "Enum repr works for flags"

main let readPerm immutable Int64 1
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0

main do printPerm
main return okCode

printPerm is call
printPerm in main
printPerm invokes console.writeIntegerLine
printPerm arg value Int64 readPerm
